  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The Department of Justice obligated $836M on contracts in FY2027 to date. The Department of Justice recorded 8,166 awards, with an average award size of $102K. Obligations fell 92.1% year over year, reflecting that current-year totals are partial (fiscal year to date). Historical context shows the Department of Justice moved from $9B in FY22 to $10B in FY23, then $9.4B in FY24, $8.6B in FY25 and $10.6B in FY26 before the current $836M in FY27. Security Guards and Patrol Services is the largest spending category in FY2027 to date at $183M, followed by General Medical and Surgical Hospitals at $104M and Other Computer Related Services at $77.7M. METROPOLITAN SECURITY SERVICES, INC. is the top vendor in FY2027 to date with $123M in obligations, followed by SCIENCE APPLICATIONS INTERNATIONAL CORPORATION at $33.1M and NAPHCARE LLC at $32.4M. All figures are contract obligations and current-year totals are partial.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How big is Justice's FY2027 contract program so far?",
        "body": "The Department of Justice obligated $836M in FY2027 to date. The Department of Justice recorded 8,166 awards, with an average award size of $102K. Obligations fell 92.1% year over year because FY2027 totals are partial. Prior annual obligations were $10.6B in FY26 and $9.4B in FY24, giving context to the partial-year total."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What are the main goods and services Justice bought this year?",
        "body": "Security Guards and Patrol Services leads FY2027 to date at $183M. The Department of Justice also obligated $104M for General Medical and Surgical Hospitals and $77.7M for Other Computer Related Services. Other notable categories include All Other Legal Services at $41.4M and Facilities Support Services at $25M."
      }
    ]
